{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520363817,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDg5NTIyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2272#issuecomment-370895227"},"message":"yes, this \"Feature\" came up with fresh 0.9.2 release from two days ago.  Some git operations really dislike having no git user.name/email configured. So now instead of waiting for things to break/work inconsistently we ask to configure git first","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520363827,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE1MDcyODkwNDA="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520364771,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDkwMDE0MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2272#issuecomment-370900141"},"message":"I think we have rushed it a bit... man git-commit-tree describes:\n```\n       While parent object ids are provided on the command line, author and\n       committer information is taken from the following environment\n       variables, if set:\n\n           GIT_AUTHOR_NAME\n           GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL\n           GIT_AUTHOR_DATE\n           GIT_COMMITTER_NAME\n           GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL\n           GIT_COMMITTER_DATE\n\n       (nb \"\u003c\", \"\u003e\" and \"\\n\"s are stripped)\n\n       In case (some of) these environment variables are not set, the\n       information is taken from the configuration items user.name and\n       user.email, or, if not present, the environment variable EMAIL, or, if\n       that is not set, system user name and the hostname used for outgoing\n       mail (taken from /etc/mailname and falling back to the fully qualified\n       hostname when that file does not exist).\n```\nso us checking for config settings only is a bit \"too crude\".\nI think, if config vars aren't defined do a quick check by issuing \"git init; git commit\" in a temp dir and detect complaints (I do not think it would be practical to track).  And then if we detect a problem we should either\n- retain current behavior and demand configuration which still will not be friendly to \"consumer\" use cases as @djarecka where authorship on commits annex etc does isn't really important\n- issue a warning, and proceed while defining a fake name/email variables (e.g. \"DataLad User\" for name and \"datalad-user@example.com\" for email) from aforementioned to be used during calls to git.  This way \"real\" users would get informed that something went wrong and bots could proceed with their needs without requiring some artifactual configuration\n\n@datalad/developers  what do you think?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1520366011,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDkwNjc0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2272#issuecomment-370906747"},"message":"Note that git annex init detects when git commit needs hand-holding,\nand sets user.name and user.email to the username. So datalad\nmight be able to avoid also needing to deal with this most annoying git\nmisfeature if it doesn't git commit before git annex init.\n\n(I've had to work around this behavior of git so many times, I'd love\nsave anyone needing to work around it once more..)\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520369176,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDkyMjE3MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2272#issuecomment-370922171"},"message":"hm, what do you mean by \"sets user.name and user.email\"?  I see no such behavior ~~(note thought that git manages to find my name from somewhere, not yet sure where from)~~\nNote: figured out that git takes the name directly from `/etc/passwd` for the user...\n\n```shell\n$\u003e mv ~/.gitconfig{,.aside}\n\n$\u003e rm -rf /tmp/testrepo; export FULLNAME= NAME= EMAIL=; mkdir /tmp/testrepo; cd /tmp/testrepo; git init; git annex init ; git show git-annex; echo 123\u003e123; git add 123; git commit -m msg\nInitialized empty Git repository in /tmp/testrepo/.git/\ninit  ok\n(recording state in git...)\ncommit 54e29af2d93f95ec351fb113320eaf99594bbd56 (git-annex)\nAuthor: Yaroslav Halchenko \u003cyoh@hopa.kiewit.dartmouth.edu\u003e\nDate:   Tue Mar 6 15:44:55 2018 -0500\n\n    update\n\ndiff --git a/uuid.log b/uuid.log\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0fc14bc\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/uuid.log\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+4bbba2fe-d086-4df3-ae5e-d7adca616878 yoh@hopa:/tmp/testrepo timestamp=1520369095.72274621s\n[master (root-commit) 2d470ca] msg\n Committer: Yaroslav Halchenko \u003cyoh@hopa.kiewit.dartmouth.edu\u003e\nYour name and email address were configured automatically based\non your username and hostname. Please check that they are accurate.\nYou can suppress this message by setting them explicitly:\n\n    git config --global user.name \"Your Name\"\n    git config --global user.email you@example.com\n\nAfter doing this, you may fix the identity used for this commit with:\n\n    git commit --amend --reset-author\n\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)\n create mode 100644 123\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1520371907,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MDkzNTYyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2272#issuecomment-370935620"},"message":"It's done in Annex/Init.hs by ensureCommit if the git-annex branch\ncreation commit fails.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1521152593,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MzU0MTg1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2272#issuecomment-373541859"},"message":"addressed by #2299 -- should allow (and just warn) an unconfigured git -- things should still work in the basic set of usecases","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1521152594,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTUyNDQyMjM0OA=="},"status":2}]}